# Environment variables Keycloak reads from deploy/local/keycloak.env (gitignored, never commit real
# values). This file is committed as a reference of what to fill in; scripts/generate-dev-secrets.sh
# creates the real gitignored file for local development automatically.
#
# ---- Auto-generated by scripts/generate-dev-secrets.sh -- do not fill in by hand ----
# KC_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_USERNAME=admin
# KC_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=<random>
# KC_DB_PASSWORD=<random>
# EDU_CRM_CLIENT_SECRET=<random>
# EDU_CRM_DEMO_USER_PASSWORD=<random>
# EDU_CRM_DEMO_SUPERVISOR_PASSWORD=<random>
# EDU_CRM_DEMO_ADMIN_PASSWORD=<random>

# ---- reCAPTCHA v2 on the Keycloak registration form (deploy/keycloak/configure-recaptcha.py, D-158) ----
# Local-dev-safe default: Google's own published "always pass" test key pair
# (https://developers.google.com/recaptcha/docs/faq) -- fine for local dev and CI, but every visitor sees
# a red "for testing purposes only" banner on the widget. Get real keys at
# https://www.google.com/recaptcha/admin/create (type: reCAPTCHA v2, "I'm not a robot" checkbox) and put
# them ONLY here before any non-local deployment. The secret key must never be committed.
RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=6LeIxAcTAAAAAJcZVRqyHh71UMIEGNQ_MXjiZKhI
RECAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY=6LeIxAcTAAAAAGG-vFI1TnRWxMZNFuojJ4WifJWe

# ---- SMTP for email verification and password reset (realm-edu-crm.json smtpServer, D-159) ----
# Local-dev default (commented out): the Mailpit catcher in compose.yaml (SMTP_HOST defaults to
# "mailpit", port 1025, no auth) -- registration and verification work with zero setup; read captured
# mail at http://localhost:8025 or its API. Uncomment and fill in for a real mailbox; never put real
# credentials anywhere but this gitignored file.
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_FROM=noreply@example.ru
# SMTP_SSL=false
# SMTP_STARTTLS=true
# SMTP_AUTH=true
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASSWORD=
